>> Learning to put every fruit in the red bin

The objective now ignores fruit identity: both apples and bananas belong in the
red bin. The yellow bin is a distractor. Each training episode starts with one
fruit already waiting at the sensor, with independently seeded position jitter
of up to 8 mm. This separates manipulation learning from the belt's automatic
arrival controller shown above.

The agent chooses among nine actions: move the grasp point by 30 mm along one
of the six Cartesian directions, close the gripper, open it, or wait. Numerical
inverse kinematics converts each motion into the real URDF joint coordinates;
position servos respect the joint limits and a 1.5 rad/s rate limit. The gripper
moves at at most 0.08 m/s. There are no automatic reach, carry or deposit actions:
the policy must choose its motions and decide when to grasp and release.

We use tabular [Q-learning|https://www.gatsby.ucl.ac.uk/~dayan/papers/cjch.pdf]
with learning rate 0.3, discount 0.98 and epsilon-greedy exploration at 0.25.
The state table records the Cartesian command cell and whether the fruit is
held. Continuous joint/tool/fruit observations remain available through the
environment API. Fruit identity is deliberately absent from the policy input.
The table is a compact state abstraction for this workcell, rather than a
vision policy or a claim of general manipulation capability.

Each decision costs 0.05; a blocked move costs another 0.15. A released fruit
that settles on the red-bin floor earns 10; a failed release or lost fruit earns
-3. [Potential-based shaping|https://ai.stanford.edu/~ang/papers/shaping-icml99.pdf]
adds `0.98 * Phi(next) - Phi(current)`, using distance to the fruit before a
grasp and distance to a point over the red bin while holding it. Absorbing
states have zero potential. Shaping supplies feedback without choosing actions.
Episodes end at release/loss or after 80 decisions, with termination and time
limits reported separately.

The next block trains from scratch, saves and reloads the final checkpoint,
and evaluates its frozen greedy policy on 128 separate seeds in an independent
environment. It also measures
an untrained random-action baseline. The video replays the first successful
apple and banana from that evaluation, in that order. Those are selected
successful examples; the printed evaluation counts include every failure.

```{cpp, results="markdown", nix-shell="git+file:../../..#cpp", cmd="c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && {bin}"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <chrono>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <fstream>
#include <numeric>
#include <optional>
#include <random>
#include <stdexcept>

int main() {
  namespace fs = std::filesystem;
  using Env = dm::sim::DevArmPickEnvironment;
  using Action = dm::sim::PickAction;
  fs::create_directories("build/fruit_sorting_rl/frames");
  fs::create_directories("figures");
  const auto assets = dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm", "../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
  const auto urdf = (fs::path(assets) / "Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string();
  Env task(urdf, 80);
  constexpr std::uint64_t training_seed = 20261101, evaluation_seed = 9000000000ULL;
  constexpr int training_episodes = 2000, evaluations = 128, baseline_episodes = 64;

  // Baseline and evaluation share initial-state seeds. Neither affects training RNGs.
  std::mt19937_64 random(1789);
  std::uniform_int_distribution<int> random_action(0, 8);
  int baseline_successes = 0;
  for (int n = 0; n < baseline_episodes; ++n) {
    auto s = task.reset(evaluation_seed + n);
    while (!s.terminated && !s.truncated) s = task.step(Action(random_action(random)));
    baseline_successes += s.success;
  }
  const auto start = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  Env training_task(urdf, 80);
  auto trained = dm::sim::train_red_bin(training_task, training_episodes, training_seed);
  const double training_seconds = std::chrono::duration<double>(
    std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - start).count();
  trained.policy.save("build/fruit_sorting_rl/policy.txt");
  const auto policy = dm::sim::PickPolicy::load("build/fruit_sorting_rl/policy.txt");
  if (policy.q != trained.policy.q) throw std::runtime_error("Checkpoint round trip changed Q values");

  std::ofstream training_csv("build/fruit_sorting_rl/training.csv");
  training_csv << "episode,return,success\n";
  for (int n = 0; n < training_episodes; ++n)
    training_csv << std::format("{},{:.9f},{}\n", n+1, trained.returns[n], int(trained.successes[n]));
  std::vector<double> episodes, rates;
  for (int end = 100; end <= training_episodes; end += 100) {
    episodes.push_back(end);
    rates.push_back(std::accumulate(trained.successes.begin()+end-100,
      trained.successes.begin()+end, 0) / 100.0);
  }
  auto curve = dm::Plot().lines(episodes, rates, "Exploratory training");
  curve.set_xlab("Training episode").set_ylab("Fraction placed into red").ylim(0, 1);
  dm::plot(curve).title("Learning to place either fruit into the red bin")
    .size(900, 340).save_svg("build/fruit_sorting_rl/learning.svg");

  std::array<int, 2> attempts{}, successes{};
  std::array<std::optional<std::uint64_t>, 2> selected;
  std::ofstream evaluation_csv("build/fruit_sorting_rl/evaluation.csv");
  evaluation_csv << "seed,fruit,success,decisions,seconds,x,y,z\n";
  for (int n = 0; n < evaluations; ++n) {
    const std::uint64_t seed = evaluation_seed + n;
    auto s = task.reset(seed);
    const int kind = s.kind == dm::sim::FruitKind::Apple ? 0 : 1;
    ++attempts[kind];
    while (!s.terminated && !s.truncated) s = task.step(policy.action(s.state));
    successes[kind] += s.success;
    if (s.success && !selected[kind]) selected[kind] = seed;
    evaluation_csv << std::format("{},{},{},{},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f}\n",
      seed, kind == 0 ? "apple" : "banana", s.success ? 1 : 0, s.decisions,
      s.time, s.fruit.x, s.fruit.y, s.fruit.z);
  }
  if (!selected[0] || !selected[1])
    throw std::runtime_error("The final policy did not solve both fruit types; no success video fabricated");
  if (successes[0] + successes[1] < .9 * evaluations)
    throw std::runtime_error("Held-out success below 90%; inspect evaluation.csv before presenting this policy");

  // Render actual recorded joint/fruit trajectories from the reloaded frozen policy.
  dm::cad::Camera camera;
  camera.position = {-1.65, -2.10, 3.40}; camera.target = {-.10, 0, .78};
  camera.projection = dm::cad::Projection::Orthographic; camera.ortho_height = 1.95;
  dm::cad::RenderOptions options;
  options.width = 960; options.height = 640; options.samples = 1;
  options.background = {.91f, .94f, .96f, 1};
  auto scenery = task.static_scene();
  dm::cad::Light key; key.direction = {-1, -2, 3}; key.intensity = 1;
  dm::cad::Light fill; fill.direction = {1, 1, 2}; fill.intensity = .35f;
  scenery.AddLight(key); scenery.AddLight(fill);
  const auto background = dm::cad::render(scenery, camera, options);
  std::ofstream trajectory("build/fruit_sorting_rl/trajectory.csv");
  trajectory << "video_frame,episode,seed,sim_seconds,grasped,success,tool_x,tool_y,tool_z,fruit_x,fruit_y,fruit_z,q1,q2,q3,q4,q5,q6,finger\n";
  int frame_number = 0;
  for (int kind = 0; kind < 2; ++kind) {
    std::vector<dm::sim::PickObservation> frames;
    task.record([&](const auto& frame) { frames.push_back(frame); });
    auto s = task.reset(*selected[kind]);
    while (!s.terminated && !s.truncated) s = task.step(policy.action(s.state));
    task.record({});
    if (!s.success) throw std::runtime_error("Frozen-policy replay did not reproduce its evaluation success");
    for (int hold = 0; hold < 24; ++hold) frames.push_back(s);
    for (const auto& frame : frames) {
      auto moving = task.dynamic_scene(frame);
      moving.lights = scenery.lights;
      const auto foreground = dm::cad::render(moving, camera, options);
      auto image = background;
      for (std::size_t pixel = 0; pixel < image.depth.size(); ++pixel)
        if (foreground.depth[pixel] < image.depth[pixel])
          std::copy_n(foreground.rgba.begin()+4*pixel, 4, image.rgba.begin()+4*pixel);
      image.save(std::format("build/fruit_sorting_rl/frames/{:05}.png", frame_number));
      if (&frame == &frames.back()) image.save("build/fruit_sorting_rl/poster.png");
      trajectory << std::format("{},{},{},{:.8f},{},{},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f}",
        frame_number++, kind+1, *selected[kind], frame.time, frame.grasped ? 1 : 0,
        frame.success ? 1 : 0, frame.tool.x, frame.tool.y, frame.tool.z,
        frame.fruit.x, frame.fruit.y, frame.fruit.z);
      for (double q : frame.joints) trajectory << std::format(",{:.9f}", q);
      trajectory << std::format(",{:.9f}\n", frame.finger);
    }
  }
  const std::string encode = "ffmpeg -hide_banner -loglevel error -y -framerate 24 "
    "-i build/fruit_sorting_rl/frames/%05d.png -frames:v " + std::to_string(frame_number) +
    " -an -c:v libx264 -profile:v baseline -level 3.1 -bf 0 -g 48 -preset fast "
    "-crf 19 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart build/fruit_sorting_rl/success.mp4";
  if (std::system(encode.c_str()) != 0) throw std::runtime_error("Could not encode learned-policy video");

  std::ofstream metrics("build/fruit_sorting_rl/metrics.json");
  metrics << std::format("{{\"algorithm\":\"tabular_q_learning\",\"training_seed\":{},"
    "\"training_episodes\":{},\"training_seconds\":{:.3f},\"baseline_successes\":{},"
    "\"baseline_episodes\":{},\"evaluation_seed\":{},\"evaluation_episodes\":{},"
    "\"apple_successes\":{},\"apple_attempts\":{},\"banana_successes\":{},\"banana_attempts\":{},"
    "\"video_apple_seed\":{},\"video_banana_seed\":{},\"video_frames\":{},\"fps\":24}}\n",
    training_seed, training_episodes, training_seconds, baseline_successes, baseline_episodes,
    evaluation_seed, evaluations, successes[0], attempts[0], successes[1], attempts[1],
    *selected[0], *selected[1], frame_number);
  training_csv.close(); evaluation_csv.close(); trajectory.close(); metrics.close();
  for (const std::string name : {"success.mp4", "poster.png", "learning.svg", "policy.txt",
      "training.csv", "evaluation.csv", "trajectory.csv", "metrics.json"})
    fs::copy_file("build/fruit_sorting_rl/"+name, "figures/fruit_sorting_rl_"+name,
      fs::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::println("After **{} training episodes**, the frozen policy placed **{}/{} apples** and "
    "**{}/{} bananas** into the red bin on separate evaluation seeds. "
    "The random-action baseline completed **{}/{}** episodes.\n",
    training_episodes, successes[0], attempts[0], successes[1], attempts[1],
    baseline_successes, baseline_episodes);
  std::println("The selected successful replays use apple seed `{}` and banana seed `{}`. "
    "Both execute the reloaded policy without exploration or scripted corrections.\n",
    *selected[0], *selected[1]);
  std::println("\\video(figures/fruit_sorting_rl_success.mp4)");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
After **2000 training episodes**, the frozen policy placed **67/67 apples** and **61/61 bananas** into the red bin on separate evaluation seeds. The random-action baseline completed **0/64** episodes.

The selected successful replays use apple seed `9000000001` and banana seed `9000000000`. Both execute the reloaded policy without exploration or scripted corrections.

