`PickPolicy::load` supports inference without retraining.

>> What this first learning environment models

The policy controls the real DevArm's joint poses through a kinematic Cartesian
position servo. Fruit motion, gravity, conveyor/bin contacts and post-release
settling use the native rigid-body engine at 240 Hz. A close command near the
fruit creates an ideal stabilized grasp with a size-dependent finger aperture;
a missed grasp reopens. Payload orientation stays stabilized during transport.
Opening restores a dynamic body, and success requires a released fruit to settle
inside the red bin with low speed and physical floor support. Merely closing the
gripper, hovering above the bin, or moving the fruit while held cannot succeed.

This model uses conservative tool/payload collision guards. It does not yet
model full arm self-collision, motor torques, slip, deformable fruit, noisy vision
or hardware timing. The camera rendering includes the actual CAD arm and depth
occlusion; cached static scenery receives no moving-object shadows. The reported
success rate describes this simplified workcell and its two fruit proxies, not
a hardware transfer result.

Source model: [Seeed reBot DevArm|https://github.com/Seeed-Projects/reBot-DevArm],
revision `922c5fa3d8c8919db1847b49166f02fc26c8fdad`, B601-DM.
`dm::datasets::fetch` downloads missing assets and verifies the pinned hashes.
The hardware assets are © 2026 Seeed Studio Co., Ltd., CERN-OHL-W-2.0;
the downloaded license remains alongside the cached model.

>> Wrist-camera vision with varied fruit and visible localization

We assign **apples to red** and **bananas to yellow** using a camera rigidly
mounted to the real DevArm's `end_link`. The classifier receives only RGB
pixels; its prediction chooses the destination before the first arm action.

Each class has **six geometry prototypes**: apples vary in girth, taper and
lobing; bananas vary in length, curvature and thickness. Each new fruit receives
an independent scale from 0.85 to 1.15, mottled skin texture, material roughness,
optional apple leaf, full-turn random yaw and small pitch/roll tilts. Both
classes draw from the same green, yellow, red/russet and brown palette.
A fruit enters at a random position along and across the belt, then travels
under friction until the optical sensor stops it. Rendered orientation and
size follow the physical proxy. Rotation remains stabilized after spawning,
as in the manipulation baseline; this is not a rolling/deformable-fruit model.

The blue wrist camera follows actual joint kinematics and never aims using
fruit coordinates or labels. Its fixed local mount is `(-0.09,-0.075,0.045)` m,
viewing local `(0.13,0,0)` with local +Z up. We use a 95-degree field of view
and 128 by 128 RGB pixels to accommodate off-centre arrivals and long bananas.

A **calibrated RGB background-subtraction localizer** compares the camera view
with a registered empty workcell at the same arm pose, including its moving
tread marks. It uses RGB differences, without reading object IDs, depth,
fruit coordinates or labels. The green box bounds the visible foreground.
Its square, padded crop is resized to 64 by 64 and supplied to MobileNet.
Boxes and prediction borders are drawn afterward for display. This localizer
assumes known synthetic scenery; it is not a trained object detector and does
not establish robustness to arbitrary backgrounds.

The full [MobileNet-v1|https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.04861] uses width 0.125,
all thirteen depthwise/pointwise blocks, ReLU6, BN and global average pooling.
All 57,738 parameters are trained from scratch with native Adam/autograd.
Training includes brightness jitter and 25% grayscale augmentation. We also
report grayscale test accuracy to check reliance on color.

We render **1,024 training scenes from prototypes 0–3**, **256 validation
scenes from prototype 4**, and **256 test scenes from prototype 5**, balanced
by class and training prototype. Seed ranges are disjoint; validation loss
selects the checkpoint and test prototypes never supply classifier gradients. This is a
stronger check than changing the seed of the same geometry. The manifest
records each seed, inspection position, sampled appearance parameters and visible bounding box.

Both placement policies are retrained for 8,000 randomized episodes each.
Motor training uses all six prototypes with independent seeds; the prototype
holdout applies to the image classifier.
The motor state adds five observed across-belt position bins before grasp;
carrying states are shared. The servo aligns the jaws to the banana proxy's
short axis and sizes its aperture to the payload. These motor controls still
use simulator geometry and the stabilized proximity grasp; fruit pose is not
estimated by the image classifier. There is no ground-truth class routing or
corrective fallback. End-to-end evaluation includes every held-out test scene;
the demonstration video then selects two successful examples of each class.

```{cpp, results="markdown", nix-shell="git+file:../../..#cpp", cmd="c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 {bin}"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/parallel.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <fstream>
#include <optional>
#include <iostream>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace s = dm::sim;

// Raw camera RGB only: labels and display annotations are never model inputs.
n::Tensor rgb(const dm::cad::RenderResult& frame) {
  std::vector<float> pixels;
  pixels.reserve(frame.width * frame.height * 3);
  for (std::size_t p = 0; p < frame.rgba.size(); p += 4)
    for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) pixels.push_back(frame.rgba[p+c] / 255.f);
  return n::from_vector(pixels, {1, frame.height, frame.width, 3});
}
struct Data { n::Tensor images, labels; std::vector<std::uint64_t> seeds; };
// Feed under contact physics, wait at the optical sensor, then settle before inspection.
s::PickObservation arrive(s::DevArmPickEnvironment& task,std::uint64_t seed) {
  auto state=task.reset_feed(seed);
  for(int i=0;i<1000 && state.feed_stage==s::ConveyorStage::Travelling;++i)
    state=task.advance_feed(1./120);
  if(state.feed_stage!=s::ConveyorStage::Waiting)throw std::runtime_error("Fruit did not arrive");
  for(int i=0;i<24;++i)state=task.advance_feed(1./120);
  return state;
}
Data camera_data(s::DevArmPickEnvironment& task,s::DevArmWristCamera& camera,
                 std::uint64_t first_seed,int per_class_prototype,int first_prototype,
                 int last_prototype,const std::string& split,std::ostream& manifest) {
  std::vector<float> pixels; std::vector<std::int64_t> labels;
  std::vector<std::uint64_t> seeds;
  std::array<std::array<int,6>,2> counts{};
  const int target=2*(last_prototype-first_prototype+1)*per_class_prototype;
  for(std::uint64_t seed=first_seed;int(seeds.size())<target;++seed){
    const auto sampled=task.reset_feed(seed);
    const int truth=sampled.kind==s::FruitKind::Apple ? 0:1;
    const int prototype=sampled.appearance.prototype;
    if(prototype<first_prototype || prototype>last_prototype || counts[truth][prototype]>=per_class_prototype)continue;
    const auto frame=arrive(task,seed);const auto inspection=camera.inspect(frame);
    if(inspection.crop.rgba.empty())throw std::runtime_error("Inspection RGB localizer missed fruit");
    auto image=rgb(inspection.crop).to_vector<float>();
    pixels.insert(pixels.end(),image.begin(),image.end());labels.push_back(truth);seeds.push_back(seed);
    ++counts[truth][prototype];
    manifest<<std::format("{},{},{},{},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.5f},{:.5f},{:.5f},{},{},{},{},{}\n",
      split,seed,truth,prototype,frame.fruit.x,frame.fruit.y,frame.appearance.yaw,
      frame.appearance.pitch,frame.appearance.scale,frame.appearance.skin[0],frame.appearance.skin[1],
      frame.appearance.skin[2],inspection.box.x,inspection.box.y,inspection.box.width,inspection.box.height,
      inspection.foreground_pixels);
    if(seeds.size()%128==0)std::cerr<<split<<" images "<<seeds.size()<<"/"<<target<<'\n';
  }
  return {n::from_vector(pixels,{target,64,64,3}),n::from_vector(labels),seeds};
}
// Display annotation only: model crops are taken before drawing any rectangle.
void box(dm::cad::RenderResult& image,const s::ImageBox& b,std::array<unsigned char,3> color){
  if(!b.width||!b.height)return;
  for(int y=b.y;y<b.y+b.height;++y)for(int x=b.x;x<b.x+b.width;++x){
    if(x>=b.x+2&&x<b.x+b.width-2&&y>=b.y+2&&y<b.y+b.height-2)continue;
    for(int c=0;c<3;++c)image.rgba[4*(y*image.width+x)+c]=color[c];
  }
}
n::Tensor grayscale(const n::Tensor& images){
  auto values=images.to_vector<float>();
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<values.size();i+=3){float y=.299f*values[i]+.587f*values[i+1]+.114f*values[i+2];values[i]=values[i+1]=values[i+2]=y;}
  return n::from_vector(values,images.shape());
}
void append(dm::cad::Scene& scene, dm::cad::Scene extra) {
  const int mesh_base = int(scene.meshes.size()), texture_base = int(scene.textures.size());
  for (auto& mesh : extra.meshes) scene.meshes.push_back(std::move(mesh));
  for (auto& texture : extra.textures) scene.textures.push_back(std::move(texture));
  for (auto object : extra.objects) {
    object.mesh_index += mesh_base; object.parent = -1;
    for (int* slot : {&object.texture_index, &object.normal_map_index,
                      &object.roughness_map_index, &object.metallic_map_index})
      if (*slot >= 0) *slot += texture_base;
    scene.AddObject(object);
  }
}

int main() {
  namespace fs = std::filesystem;
  n::set_num_threads(1);
  fs::create_directories("build/fruit_vision/frames");
  fs::create_directories("figures");
  const auto assets = dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm", "../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
  const auto urdf = (fs::path(assets)/"Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string();
  s::DevArmPickEnvironment task(urdf,100,s::FruitVariation::Diverse);
  s::DevArmWristCamera wrist(task,128,95);
  std::ofstream manifest("build/fruit_vision/image_manifest.csv");
  manifest << "split,seed,label_0_apple_1_banana,prototype,x,y,yaw,pitch,scale,red,green,blue,box_x,box_y,box_width,box_height,foreground_pixels\n";
  const auto training=camera_data(task,wrist,12000000000ULL,128,0,3,"training",manifest);
  const auto validation=camera_data(task,wrist,13000000000ULL,128,4,4,"validation",manifest);
  const auto test=camera_data(task,wrist,14000000000ULL,128,5,5,"test",manifest);
  manifest.close();
  n::save_image_grid(n::slice_axis(test.images,0,0,24),"build/fruit_vision/camera_samples.png",8,0,1,2,.9,2);
  // One actual wrist image for each of the twelve geometry prototypes.
  std::array<std::array<std::optional<std::uint64_t>,6>,2> gallery{};
  for(unsigned seed=0;seed<1000;++seed){auto f=task.reset_feed(seed);gallery[int(f.kind)][f.appearance.prototype]=seed;}
  std::vector<float> gallery_pixels;
  for(int fruit=0;fruit<2;++fruit)for(int prototype=0;prototype<6;++prototype){
    const auto f=arrive(task,*gallery[fruit][prototype]);auto v=wrist.inspect(f);box(v.rgb,v.box,{30,245,120});
    const auto pixels=rgb(v.rgb).to_vector<float>();gallery_pixels.insert(gallery_pixels.end(),pixels.begin(),pixels.end());
  }
  n::save_image_grid(n::from_vector(gallery_pixels,{12,128,128,3}),"build/fruit_vision/prototypes.png",6,0,1,2,.9,1);

  n::MobileNetClassifier model(2,64,.125,20261103);
  n::MobileClassifierOptions options;
  options.epochs=40; options.batch_size=16; options.seed=20261103;
  options.grayscale_probability=.25;
  const auto fitted = model.fit(training.images,training.labels,
    validation.images,validation.labels,options);
  model.save("build/fruit_vision/mobilenet.npz");
  auto classifier = n::MobileNetClassifier::load("build/fruit_vision/mobilenet.npz");
  const auto probabilities = classifier.predict(test.images);
  if (n::max(n::abs(probabilities-model.predict(test.images))).item() > 1e-7)
    throw std::runtime_error("MobileNet checkpoint changed inference");
  const auto predicted = n::argmax(probabilities,-1);
  n::ConfusionMatrix confusion(2); confusion.add(test.labels,predicted);
  n::ConfusionMatrixPlotOptions confusion_options;
  confusion_options.labels={"Apple","Banana"}; confusion_options.cell_size=100;
  confusion_options.title="Wrist RGB: held-out prototype 5";
  confusion.save_svg("build/fruit_vision/confusion.svg",confusion_options);

  std::ofstream fit_csv("build/fruit_vision/classifier_training.csv");
  fit_csv << "epoch,training_loss,validation_loss,validation_accuracy\n";
  std::vector<double> epochs, train_loss, validation_loss, accuracy;
  for (const auto& row : fitted.history) {
    epochs.push_back(row.epoch); train_loss.push_back(row.training_loss);
    validation_loss.push_back(row.validation_loss); accuracy.push_back(row.validation_accuracy);
    fit_csv << std::format("{},{:.9f},{:.9f},{:.9f}\n",row.epoch,
      row.training_loss,row.validation_loss,row.validation_accuracy);
  }
  fit_csv.close();
  auto losses=dm::Plot().lines(epochs,train_loss,"Training",dm::RGB{37,99,235});
  losses.lines(epochs,validation_loss,"Validation",dm::RGB{220,38,38});
  losses.set_title("Cross entropy").set_xlab("Epoch").set_ylab("Loss");
  auto valid_accuracy=dm::Plot().lines(epochs,accuracy,"Validation",dm::RGB{15,140,100});
  valid_accuracy.set_title("Validation accuracy").set_xlab("Epoch").set_ylab("Correct fraction").ylim(0,1);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(losses).add(valid_accuracy).fit_panels();
  dm::plot(layout).size(1050,340).save_svg("build/fruit_vision/classifier_learning.svg");

  const auto gray_predictions=n::argmax(classifier.predict(grayscale(test.images)),-1).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto truths=test.labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  int gray_correct=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<truths.size();++i)gray_correct+=gray_predictions[i]==truths[i];
  // Train both motor policies afresh for randomized sizes, orientations and lateral bins.
  s::DevArmPickEnvironment training_task(urdf,100,s::FruitVariation::Diverse);
  auto learn=[&](s::PickBin goal,const std::string& name){
    std::cerr<<"Learning "<<name<<" policy\n";
    const auto learned=s::train_pick_bin(training_task,goal,8000,20261105);
    learned.policy.save("build/fruit_vision/"+name+"_policy.txt");
    const auto restored=s::PickPolicy::load("build/fruit_vision/"+name+"_policy.txt");
    if(restored.q!=learned.policy.q)throw std::runtime_error("Q checkpoint changed values");
    std::ofstream csv("build/fruit_vision/"+name+"_training.csv");csv<<"episode,return,success\n";
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<learned.returns.size();++i)csv<<std::format("{},{:.9f},{}\n",i+1,learned.returns[i],int(learned.successes[i]));
    return restored;
  };
  const auto red=learn(s::PickBin::Red,"red"),yellow=learn(s::PickBin::Yellow,"yellow");
  std::array<int,2> totals{},classified{},sorted{},placed{};
  std::array<std::vector<std::uint64_t>,2> selected;
  std::ofstream evaluation("build/fruit_vision/evaluation.csv");
  evaluation<<"seed,prototype,true_class,predicted_class,confidence,destination,goal_placement,correct_sort,decisions,x,y,z\n";
  for(const auto seed:test.seeds){
    auto state=arrive(task,seed);const auto inspection=wrist.inspect(state);
    const auto p=classifier.predict(rgb(inspection.crop)).to_vector<float>();
    const int prediction=p[1]>p[0]?1:0;
    task.set_destination(prediction==0?s::PickBin::Red:s::PickBin::Yellow);
    const auto& policy=prediction==0?red:yellow;
    while(!state.terminated&&!state.truncated)state=task.step(policy.action(state.state));
    const int truth=state.kind==s::FruitKind::Apple?0:1;
    ++totals[truth];classified[truth]+=prediction==truth;placed[truth]+=state.success;
    const bool correct=state.success&&prediction==truth;sorted[truth]+=correct;
    if(correct&&selected[truth].size()<2)selected[truth].push_back(seed);
    evaluation<<std::format("{},{},{},{},{:.9f},{},{},{},{},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f}\n",seed,state.appearance.prototype,
      truth,prediction,p[prediction],prediction==0?"red":"yellow",int(state.success),int(correct),state.decisions,state.fruit.x,state.fruit.y,state.fruit.z);
  }
  evaluation.close();
  if(selected[0].size()<2||selected[1].size()<2)throw std::runtime_error("Insufficient successful examples for video");
  std::cerr<<"Evaluation: classifier "<<classified[0]+classified[1]<<"/256, sorting "<<sorted[0]+sorted[1]<<"/256\n";

  // A steep overview makes both bin interiors visible; the inset remains a real wrist view.
  dm::cad::Camera overview;
  overview.position={-1.35,-.6,5.0}; overview.target={-.10,0,.70};
  overview.projection=dm::cad::Projection::Orthographic; overview.ortho_height=1.95;
  dm::cad::RenderOptions render_options;
  render_options.width=960; render_options.height=640;
  render_options.background={.91f,.94f,.96f,1};
  auto scenery=task.static_scene();
  dm::cad::Light key; key.direction={-1,-2,3}; key.intensity=1; scenery.AddLight(key);
  dm::cad::Light fill; fill.direction={1,1,2}; fill.intensity=.35f; scenery.AddLight(fill);
  const auto background=dm::cad::render(scenery,overview,render_options);
  std::ofstream trajectory("build/fruit_vision/trajectory.csv");
  trajectory << "frame,episode,seed,predicted_class,target,sim_seconds,grasped,success,fruit_x,fruit_y,fruit_z,q1,q2,q3,q4,q5,q6,finger\n";
  int frame_number=0;
  for(int episode=0;episode<4;++episode){
    const auto seed=selected[episode%2][episode/2];
    std::vector<s::PickObservation> feeding;
    task.record([&](const auto& f){feeding.push_back(f);});
    auto state=arrive(task,seed);task.record({});
    const auto p=classifier.predict(rgb(wrist.inspect(state).crop)).to_vector<float>();
    const int prediction=p[1]>p[0]?1:0;
    task.set_destination(prediction==0?s::PickBin::Red:s::PickBin::Yellow);
    // Speed up feeding fourfold in the video; manipulation stays at real time.
    std::vector<s::PickObservation> frames;
    for(std::size_t k=0;k<feeding.size();k+=4)frames.push_back(feeding[k]);
    frames.push_back(state);
    task.record([&](const auto& f){frames.push_back(f);});
    const auto& policy=prediction==0?red:yellow;
    while(!state.terminated&&!state.truncated)state=task.step(policy.action(state.state));
    task.record({});
    if(!state.success||prediction!=(state.kind==s::FruitKind::Apple?0:1))throw std::runtime_error("Replay failed");
    for(int hold=0;hold<24;++hold)frames.push_back(state);
    std::array<double,6> last_joints{};double last_finger=-1;
    auto base=background;
    for(const auto& frame:frames){
      if(frame.joints!=last_joints||frame.finger!=last_finger){
        auto arm=task.robot_scene(frame);append(arm,wrist.housing(frame));arm.lights=scenery.lights;
        const auto rendered=dm::cad::render(arm,overview,render_options);base=background;
        for(std::size_t i=0;i<base.depth.size();++i)if(rendered.depth[i]<base.depth[i]){
          std::copy_n(rendered.rgba.begin()+4*i,4,base.rgba.begin()+4*i);base.depth[i]=rendered.depth[i];
        }
        last_joints=frame.joints;last_finger=frame.finger;
      }
      auto moving=task.fruit_scene(frame);moving.lights=scenery.lights;
      const auto actors=dm::cad::render(moving,overview,render_options);auto image=base;
      for(std::size_t i=0;i<image.depth.size();++i)if(actors.depth[i]<image.depth[i])
        std::copy_n(actors.rgba.begin()+4*i,4,image.rgba.begin()+4*i);
      auto inspection=wrist.inspect(frame);
      // Green rectangle is the live RGB localizer; red/yellow border is the latched prediction.
      box(inspection.rgb,inspection.box,{30,245,120});
      constexpr int scale=2,left=684,top=20,border=5;
      const std::array<unsigned char,3> color{static_cast<unsigned char>(prediction==0?210:250),static_cast<unsigned char>(prediction==0?40:210),35};
      for(int y=-border;y<128*scale+border;++y)for(int x=-border;x<128*scale+border;++x){
        const auto i=4*((top+y)*image.width+left+x);const bool edge=x<0||y<0||x>=128*scale||y>=128*scale;
        for(int c=0;c<3;++c)image.rgba[i+c]=edge?color[c]:inspection.rgb.rgba[4*((y/scale)*128+x/scale)+c];
        image.rgba[i+3]=255;
      }
      image.save(std::format("build/fruit_vision/frames/{:05}.png",frame_number));
      if(frame_number==int(feeding.size()/4)+1&&episode==0)image.save("build/fruit_vision/inspection.png");
      if(&frame==&frames.back())image.save("build/fruit_vision/poster.png");
      trajectory<<std::format("{},{},{},{},{},{:.8f},{},{},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f}",frame_number++,episode+1,seed,
        prediction,prediction==0?"red":"yellow",frame.time,int(frame.grasped),int(frame.success),frame.fruit.x,frame.fruit.y,frame.fruit.z);
      for(double q:frame.joints)trajectory<<std::format(",{:.9f}",q);trajectory<<std::format(",{:.9f}\n",frame.finger);
    }
  }
  trajectory.close();
  const auto encode="ffmpeg -hide_banner -loglevel error -y -framerate 24 "
    "-i build/fruit_vision/frames/%05d.png -frames:v "+std::to_string(frame_number)+
    " -an -c:v libx264 -profile:v baseline -level 3.1 -bf 0 -g 48 -preset fast "
    "-crf 19 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart build/fruit_vision/sorting.mp4";
  if(std::system(encode.c_str())!=0) throw std::runtime_error("Could not encode vision sorting video");
  std::ofstream metrics("build/fruit_vision/metrics.json");
  metrics<<"{\"architecture\":\"MobileNetV1\",\"parameters\":"<<classifier.parameter_count()
    <<",\"training_images\":1024,\"validation_images\":256,\"test_images\":256,\"training_prototypes\":[0,1,2,3],\"validation_prototypes\":[4],\"test_prototypes\":[5]"
    <<",\"epochs\":40,\"selected_epoch\":"<<fitted.selected_epoch<<",\"classifier_correct\":"<<classified[0]+classified[1]
    <<",\"grayscale_correct\":"<<gray_correct<<",\"correct_sorts\":"<<sorted[0]+sorted[1]
    <<",\"placements_at_predicted_goal\":"<<placed[0]+placed[1]<<",\"apple_correct_sorts\":"<<sorted[0]
    <<",\"banana_correct_sorts\":"<<sorted[1]<<",\"motor_episodes_per_goal\":8000,\"video_frames\":"<<frame_number<<",\"fps\":24}\n";
  metrics.close();
  for(const std::string name:{"sorting.mp4","poster.png","inspection.png","prototypes.png","camera_samples.png","confusion.svg",
      "classifier_learning.svg","mobilenet.npz","red_policy.txt","yellow_policy.txt","image_manifest.csv",
      "classifier_training.csv","red_training.csv","yellow_training.csv","evaluation.csv","trajectory.csv","metrics.json"})
    fs::copy_file("build/fruit_vision/"+name,"figures/fruit_vision_"+name,fs::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::println("On **256 held-out prototype-5 scenes**, MobileNet classified **{}/256** RGB crops correctly and **{}/256** grayscale crops correctly. Validation selected epoch **{}**.\n",classified[0]+classified[1],gray_correct,fitted.selected_epoch);
  std::println("Using only those class predictions for routing, the robot correctly sorted **{}/128 apples into red** and **{}/128 bananas into yellow**. All 256 attempts appear in the evaluation CSV.\n",sorted[0],sorted[1]);
  std::println("The video shows four successful held-out episodes: seeds `{}`, `{}`, `{}`, `{}`. Feeding is shown at 4x speed; arm manipulation is real time. Green rectangles are live RGB localization boxes; red/yellow inset borders show the latched MobileNet prediction.\n",selected[0][0],selected[1][0],selected[0][1],selected[1][1]);
  std::println("\\video(figures/fruit_vision_sorting.mp4)");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
On **256 held-out prototype-5 scenes**, MobileNet classified **241/256** RGB crops correctly and **236/256** grayscale crops correctly. Validation selected epoch **38**.

Using only those class predictions for routing, the robot correctly sorted **126/128 apples into red** and **115/128 bananas into yellow**. All 256 attempts appear in the evaluation CSV.

The video shows four successful held-out episodes: seeds `14000000016`, `14000000001`, `14000000023`, `14000000005`. Feeding is shown at 4x speed; arm manipulation is real time. Green rectangles are live RGB localization boxes; red/yellow inset borders show the latched MobileNet prediction.

\video(figures/fruit_vision_sorting.mp4)
// result_end

\caption(Four varied-fruit sorting examples. Feeding is accelerated fourfold; arm motion is real time. Green rectangles in the live wrist view are RGB foreground boxes. The red or yellow inset border displays the inspection prediction throughout each replayed clip.)
\alttext(Off-centre fruit with varied colors, sizes and orientations arrives on a belt. A wrist-mounted camera shows a green box around the visible fruit. The robot places predicted apples in red and predicted bananas in yellow.)

[Open the varied-fruit sorting video|file:figures/fruit_vision_sorting.mp4]
or its [final placement frame|file:figures/fruit_vision_poster.png].

\image(figures/fruit_vision_prototypes.png)
