\alttext(A robot inspects an off-centre fruit. The camera inset highlights its visible bounds.)

Run artifacts: [MobileNet checkpoint|file:figures/fruit_vision_mobilenet.npz],
[red placement policy|file:figures/fruit_vision_red_policy.txt],
[yellow placement policy|file:figures/fruit_vision_yellow_policy.txt],
[image/appearance/box manifest|file:figures/fruit_vision_image_manifest.csv],
[classifier training|file:figures/fruit_vision_classifier_training.csv],
[red-policy training|file:figures/fruit_vision_red_training.csv],
[yellow-policy training|file:figures/fruit_vision_yellow_training.csv],
[all end-to-end evaluations|file:figures/fruit_vision_evaluation.csv],
[video trajectories|file:figures/fruit_vision_trajectory.csv],
and [metrics|file:figures/fruit_vision_metrics.json].

This tests generalization within procedural simulated CAD fruit and a calibrated
workcell. It does not establish recognition of real fruit photographs or
unfamiliar backgrounds. Classification is supervised; manipulation is tabular
Q-learning with simulator geometry and idealized grasp/collision assumptions.
A wrong prediction is counted as a wrong sort even if placement succeeds.
